---
title: Definition 10
---
order: 10
---
short_label: V.Def.10
---
statement: When four magnitudes are continuously proportional, the first is said to have to the fourth the <i>triplicate ratio</i> of that which it has to the second, and so on continually, whatever be the proportion.
---
